Subject: EXTROPY: Sex in the future

Another call for articles for EXTROPY.  (Even if no one volunteers to tackle
this topic for publication, it should make an interesting thread for the list.)

I'm looking for someone to write on how sex will be affected by both near and
distant future technologies.  Some possible topics:

- Effects of VR on sexual encounters (presenting a different body/gender in the
VR realm to one's physical body).

- Use of neurochemical and hormonal modification to (a) alter intensity, 
duration, and perceived quality of sensations; and (b) alter sexual drive
(subjecting it to voluntary control).

- Cultural effects of easy and thorough sex changes.

- Effects of wide availability of interactive VR sex programs, advanced
mechanical sexual surrogates, and PGP-encrypted pornography markets (as
recently discussed here).

- Possibilities for expanded sexual experience due to radical alterations in
our bodies.  (Cf. Ettinger's speculations in "Man Into Superman" on bodies with
multiple protrusions and orifices.)

- Is sexuality important to self-transformation and a satisfying life, or is it
a hindrance?  How does sexuality fit into an extropian view of life?

- How are we to regard the prospect of human-android sexual relations? (Both 
intrinsically and considering its possible effects on the relative 
desirability of human-human relations.)

- Possibilities (as suggested on the list) of modifying the triggers for sexual
excitement, e.g., to produce orgasm upon accomplishing an important task, or
to tailor the conditions under which one becomes and stays aroused.

And so on.  I think it's time for EXTROPY to publish something on transhuman 
sex.  Many Extropians I know have a keen interest in sex, yet our published 
writings may give the appearance of an exclusively cerebral interest.


